# Cathode — standalone repository ignore rules.
#
# Carried forward in INTENT from the source tree (uptime `.gitignore:20-26` + the plugin-local
# `Authoring/.gitignore`), re-rooted for this repo's layout: the plugin lives at `Cathode/`, not
# at `game/Plugins/Cathode/`. Rules are path-anchored (leading `/`) exactly as the source's were,
# so they bind to these locations and nowhere else.

# --- Vendored third-party library SOURCE (reserved; populated by the plugin's install.sh) ---
# The 5 upstream libs (quickjs-ng, litehtml, harfbuzz, blend2d, asmjit) are cloned at pinned
# commits, never committed — install.sh reproduces them from its pin table on any checkout.
/vendor/

# --- Cathode vendor-lib BUILD OUTPUTS ---
# `include/` and `Win64/` under each ThirdParty lib are build artifacts, not source: they are
# produced by the vendor build from the gitignored `vendor/` sources. Each lib dir keeps a
# tracked `.gitkeep` (5 of them in the source tree) so the directory shape survives without its
# contents. Mirrors uptime `.gitignore:25-26`.
/Cathode/Source/ThirdParty/*/Win64/
/Cathode/Source/ThirdParty/*/include/

# --- Authoring/ Node toolchain (dev-machine/CI only) ---
# `node_modules/` and the IIFE build output `dist/` are not committed; package.json +
# package-lock.json are, for a reproducible `npm ci`. NOTE: the plugin subtree carries its own
# `Cathode/Authoring/.gitignore` with these same two rules — it arrives with the Slice 2 copy.
# These root entries are deliberate belt-and-braces so the Slice 2 copy cannot land stray
# node_modules/dist before that file is in place.
/Cathode/Authoring/node_modules/
/Cathode/Authoring/dist/
